  "text": "Home | Veterinary Medical Center\nSkip to main content\nIt looks like you're using an unsupported browser\nFor the best experience please switch to a supported browser\nChrome\nSafari\nFirefox\nEdge\nOhio State nav bar\nThe Ohio State University\nBuckeyeLink\nFind People\nWebmail\nSearch Ohio State\nOSU More Action\nVeterinary Medical Center\nCollege of Veterinary Medicine\nLocations\nGiving\nOpen Search Menu\n'I am a' Menu with links to the OSU Veterinary Medical Center and the College of Veterinary Medicine\nI am a...\nOSU Hamburger Menu\nServices\nAll Services\nCompanion Animals\nFarm\nEquine\nBy Location\nAll Services\nCompanion Animals\nFarm\nEquine\nBy Location\nClinical Trials\nCurrent Trials\nOwners\nInvestigator Support\nSponsors\nVeterinarians (rDVMs)\nSupport the BBVCTO\nCurrent Trials\nOwners\nInvestigator Support\nSponsors\nVeterinarians (rDVMs)\nSupport the BBVCTO\nReferring Veterinarians\nResources\nAbout\nCareers\nCareers\nEmergency\nServices\nBack to Main Menu\nServices\nServices Overview\nAll Services\nCompanion Animals\nFarm\nEquine\nBy Location\nClinical Trials\nBack to Main Menu\nClinical Trials\nClinical Trials Overview\nCurrent Trials\nOwners\nInvestigator Support\nSponsors\nVeterinarians (rDVMs)\nSupport the BBVCTO\nReferring Veterinarians\nResources\nAbout\nBack to Main Menu\nAbout\nAbout Overview\nCareers\nSearch Veterinary Medical Center\nSearch Site\nServices\nAll Services\nCompanion Animals\nFarm\nEquine\nBy Location\nAll Services\nCompanion Animals\nFarm\nEquine\nBy Location\nClinical Trials\nCurrent Trials\nOwners\nInvestigator Support\nSponsors\nVeterinarians (rDVMs)\nSupport the BBVCTO\nCurrent Trials\nOwners\nInvestigator Support\nSponsors\nVeterinarians (rDVMs)\nSupport the BBVCTO\nReferring Veterinarians\nResources\nAbout\nCareers\nCareers\nEmergency\nServices\nBack to Main Menu\nServices\nServices Overview\nAll Services\nCompanion Animals\nFarm\nEquine\nBy Location\nClinical Trials\nBack to Main Menu\nClinical Trials\nClinical Trials Overview\nCurrent Trials\nOwners\nInvestigator Support\nSponsors\nVeterinarians (rDVMs)\nSupport the BBVCTO\nReferring Veterinarians\nResources\nAbout\nBack to Main Menu\nAbout\nAbout Overview\nCareers\nCollege of Veterinary Medicine\nLocations\nGiving\nEmergency\nI am a...\nToggles the 'I am a' Menu with links to the OSU Veterinary Medical Center and the College of Veterinary Medicine\nBuckeyeLink\nFind People\nWebmail\nSearch Ohio State\nHero Slider\nof\nCaring. Down to a science.\nFrom routine care to complex conditions, The Ohio State University Veterinary Medical Center brings together expert veterinary teams, advanced technology and comprehensive services to help your animal live a happier, healthier life.\nLearn more about the VMC\nFind the level of care to match your animals' needs\nWe offer a wide variety of veterinary care services across six hospital locations to give your dog, cat, horse or farm animal the best treatment possible.\nExplore our available services\nSix hospitals to serve you.\nThe Ohio State University Veterinary Medical Center is comprised of six hospitals located within Columbus, Ohio and the surrounding areas of Dublin and Marysville. Our hospitals cover the full spectrum of veterinary care including primary care, urgent care, advanced specialty and emergency critical care for dogs, cats, horses and farm animals. Learn more about how each hospital is prepared to serve your animal's care needs.\nView available options within our hospital system\nAn extension of your practice\nWe are committed to continuously earning and maintaining your trust and respect as we work in partnership with you to provide the best possible care for your patients and service to your clients.\npartner with us\nFind your next career\nJoin our passionate team and embark on a rewarding career where your love for animals meets professional excellence.\nLearn about working with us\nAbout\nServices\nLocations\nreferring veterinarians\nCareers\nPrevious Slide\n/\nNext Slide\nAbout\nServices\nLocations\nreferring veterinarians\nCareers\nCaring. Down to a science.\nFrom routine care to complex conditions, The Ohio State University Veterinary Medical Center brings together expert veterinary teams, advanced technology and comprehensive services to help your animal live a happier, healthier life.\nLearn more about the VMC\nFind the level of care to match your animals' needs\nWe offer a wide variety of veterinary care services across six hospital locations to give your dog, cat, horse or farm animal the best treatment possible.\nExplore our available services\nSix hospitals to serve you.\nThe Ohio State University Veterinary Medical Center is comprised of six hospitals located within Columbus, Ohio and the surrounding areas of Dublin and Marysville. Our hospitals cover the full spectrum of veterinary care including primary care, urgent care, advanced specialty and emergency critical care for dogs, cats, horses and farm animals. Learn more about how each hospital is prepared to serve your animal's care needs.\nView available options within our hospital system\nAn extension of your practice\nWe are committed to continuously earning and maintaining your trust and respect as we work in partnership with you to provide the best possible care for your patients and service to your clients.\npartner with us\nFind your next career\nJoin our passionate team and embark on a rewarding career where your love for animals meets professional excellence.\nLearn about working with us\nConstruction and Hospital Access\nVernon L. Tharp St. remains closed at the intersection with John Herrick Drive, however, John Herrick is open to two-way traffic between Olentangy River Road and Woody Hayes Blvd.\nDue to various construction projects happening around Ohio State's campus, please check ODOT's OHGO app or click below to view real-time traffic and road closures.\nOHGO from ODOT\nOHGO from ODOT\nComprehensive, compassionate care\nAnimals provide unconditional love and enrich our lives, and we know that you want the best for your companion. At the Ohio State Veterinary Medical Center, you’ll find the highest level of professional veterinary medical care, whether your visit is for a well-check, chronic illness, urgent or emergency service. You and your dogs, cats, horses or farm animals will find comprehensive, compassionate care supported by a highly-regarded academic institution.\nCompanion\nEmergency\nVeterinary Medical Center at Dublin\n(614) 889-8070\nMap and Directions\nCompanion\nFrank Stanton Veterinary Spectrum of Care Clinic\n(614) 292-1573\nMap and Directions\nEquine\nEmergency\nGalbreath Equine Center & Ralph Rogan Equine Performance Evaluation Arena\n(614) 292-6661\nMap and Directions\nFarm\nEmergency\nHospital for Farm Animals\n(614) 292-6661\nMap and Directions\nCompanion\nEmergency\nHummel Trueman Hospital for Companion Animals\n(614) 292-3551\nMap and Directions\nEquine\nFarm\nEmergency\nLarge Animal Services at Marysville\n(937) 642-2936\nMap and Directions\nOur six hospitals by the numbers...\n60K\nVisits\n36\nServices\n640\nVMC Team Members\nPatient Success Stories\nRead more\nRead more\nPercy's Story\nTeamwork proves successful for rare equine dental surgery\nIn March 2023, members of the VMC’s Galbreath Equine Center surgical team removed a large mass from the lower jaw of an 8-year-old draft cross gelding. The procedure – a first of its kind at Ohio State – highlighted a successful collaboration among our VMC surgeons, our local equine dental specialist partner, and equine dental surgeons from Kentucky.\nRead more\nToby's Story\nNeurosurgical technique addresses dog’s herniated disc\nToby, a 6-year-old Weimaraner, presented to the VMC as an emergency referral with the inability to walk on all four legs. An MRI performed on Toby at the VMC revealed a large intervertebral disc herniation in the cervical spine, requiring surgical removal. The surgery went well and Toby recovered quickly, walking the day after surgery. He was discharged two days after surgery and continues to recover at home.\nRead more\nClinical Trials\nAll current trials\nall cancer trials\nall pathology trials\nall bones and joints trials\ncancer\nDetection of remaining cancer after tumor removal\nOur team of world-class, board-certified veterinary medical, surgical and radiation oncologists, residents and veterinary technicians are here to provide you and your pets with the most advanced and comprehensive care and treatment options to ensure the best possible quality of life for your furry family member. The Integrated Oncology Service is often recruiting patients for a number of studies for which your pet may be eligible. Please refer to each clinical trial page below for detailed information.\nall cancer trials\npathology\nPimobendan use in cats with advanced heart disease\nOur veterinary laboratory professionals provide reliable, accessible, cost-effective, efficient and innovative laboratory diagnostic testing across multiple lab sections including Applied (Anatomic) Pathology, Clinical Pathology, Microbiology, Renal Pathology and Parasitology. The collective professional expertise of the Clinical Diagnostic Laboratories supports the teaching, service and clinical research. Please refer to each clinical trial page below for detailed information.\nall pathology trials\nbones and joints\nPain management in dogs undergoing knee surgery\nThe Small Animal Orthopedic Surgery service at the Veterinary Medical Center at Ohio State offers comprehensive surgical care for dogs and cats with orthopedic conditions. Please refer to each clinical trial page below for detailed information.\nall bones and joints trials\nJoin our Team!\nBecome an integral part of a renowned academic institution where you will utilize your advanced training and skills, to help provide world-class medical care to patients of The Ohio State University Veterinary Medical Center hospitals!\nCareer Opportunities\nThe Ohio State University\nVeterinary Medical Center Facebook Page\nVeterinary Medical Center Instagram Page\nVeterinary Medical Center Twitter Page\nVeterinary Medical Center LinkedIn Page\nVeterinary Medical Center YouTube Page\nVeterinary Medical Center at Dublin\n5020 Bradenton Avenue\nDublin 43017 OH\n(614) 889-8070\nFrank Stanton Veterinary Spectrum of Care Clinic\n655 Vernon L. Tharp St\nColumbus 43210 OH\n(614) 292-1573\nGalbreath Equine Center & Ralph Rogan Equine Performance Evaluation Arena\n685 Vernon L. Tharp Street\nColumbus 43210 OH\n(614) 292-6661\nHospital for Farm Animals\n601 Vernon L. Tharp St\nColumbus 43210 OH\n(614) 292-6661\nHummel Trueman Hospital for Companion Animals\n601 Vernon L. Tharp Street\nColumbus 43210 OH\n(614) 292-3551\nLarge Animal Services at Marysville\n16410 County Home Rd\nMarysville 43040 OH\n(937) 642-2936\nHelpful Links\nCareers\nContact Us\nPay My Bill\nReferring Vets Portal\nVeterinary Medical Center Facebook Page\nVeterinary Medical Center Instagram Page\nVeterinary Medical Center Twitter Page\nVeterinary Medical Center LinkedIn Page\nVeterinary Medical Center YouTube Page\nLooking for the College of Veterinary Medicine?\nPlease Visit\nvet.osu.edu\nPlease Call\n(614) 292-1171\nNon-discrimination Notice\nPrivacy Statement\nCookie Settings\n©\n2026\nThe Ohio State University\nIf you have a disability and experience difficulty accessing this content, contact\nCVM-DigitalAccessibility@osu.edu",
